id: rust.select-timeout
kind: rust
title: tokio::select! with a timeout branch
aliases: select timeout, race a sleep, timeout branch
tags: async, tokio, timeouts, concurrency
questions:
  - how do you race a timeout against a future and cancel the loser?
invariant: In select!, the timeout branch wins when elapsed; the other branch is dropped, so its resource must be tied to a scope that handles early drop.
answer_30s: Put a tokio::time::sleep or sleep_until in a tokio::select! branch; the future you do not want completing is dropped when the timeout branch fires, which cancels it.
when_to_use:
  - bounding a single await that has no deadline-aware API
  - racing a heartbeat against a request
avoid_when:
  - the call already accepts a deadline or timeout argument (use that instead)
related:
  - rust.timeout
  - rust.cancellation
sources:
  - https://docs.rs/tokio/latest/tokio/macro.select.html
